.TH IMPROVE 1 "" "Improve 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
improve \- deterministic Ada quality remediation planning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B improve
command [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Improve reads completed Ada Quality assessments, stores immutable remediation plans, and publishes
native model_runner tasks.
.SH COMMANDS
projects, findings, plan, audit, apply, tasks, status, refresh, verify, recover, doctor, config,
completion, manpage, help, and version.
.SH PLAN OPERATIONS
plan supports list, show, approve, diff, explain, or graph in addition to deterministic generation.
.SH AUDIT
audit PLAN-ID [--revision N] exports immutable provenance, approval, publication, and verification evidence.
audit verify FILE checks its canonical digest. Signed artifacts require --verification-key FILE as an independent
trust anchor for the Ed25519 signature.
.SH OUTPUT
--format accepts terminal, json, markdown, or dot for plan graph. JSON output and JSON errors are single versioned
documents.
.SH LOCAL REFINEMENT
--agent-model, --agent-model-path, and --agent-model-sha256 override the optional local runtime. --no-agent disables
refinement for one invocation. --progress accepts auto, always, or never; auto emits runtime progress only when
standard error is a terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 unresolved verification or unhealthy diagnostics; 2 invalid input; 3 unavailable evidence; 4 storage or
internal failure; 130 interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
ada_quality(1), model_runner(1)
